From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:11:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 013/167] mobile: an enlarged cursor is drawn with its hot spot
 where it clicks

CursorPaint enlarges small cursors at low zoom but scaled the hot spot offset
with the image, so an I-beam or a hand pointed a few points away from where the
click landed. The hot spot now stays on the remote position; unchanged when
the cursor is not enlarged.

(Research patch ios-touch 0007.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart b/flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart
index 7d4bf9c..5c08b82 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/mobile/pages/remote_page.dart
@@ -1209,8 +1209,10 @@ class CursorPaint extends StatelessWidget {
     return CustomPaint(
       painter: ImagePainter(
           image: image,
-          x: (m.x - hotx) * factor + c.x / s2,
-          y: (m.y - hoty) * factor + (c.y + adjust) / s2,
+          // Drawn larger than the image (s2 > s), the cursor keeps its hot
+          // spot, not its corner, on the remote position.
+          x: m.x * factor - hotx + c.x / s2,
+          y: m.y * factor - hoty + (c.y + adjust) / s2,
           scale: s2),
     );
   }
